  <revision rev="5" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>6bed1f81ab04e520ca580deb766045ee</srcmd5>
    <version>1.3.3</version>
    <time>1793007598</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>- update to 1.3.3:
  * Add PSIS LFO-CV
  * Accept coords in ci_in_rope, as its docstring documents
  * Correct interval for pit evaluation
  * Only build the summary's LaTeX repr when asked for
  * Add bivariate histogram and hexbin statistics
  * Add ELPD subclasses
  * Add default `ci_kind` handling in `ci_in_rope`
  * Miscelaneous docstrings fixes
  * Update citation information
  * More miscellaneous docstring fixes
  * Fix ddof in `summary` std computation
  * Hexbin and histogram2d: Use adaptive binning
  * Fix histogram with array-like bins
  * Allow hdi with prob=1
- update to 1.3.2:
  * ### Maintenance and bug fixes
  * Respect ci_kind in summary for the stats and all kinds
  * Remove deprecated inplace in sort_values
  * Write the bandwidth into the kde gufunc output
  * Ensure correct order for bounds in circular std
  * Add PyMC and Bambi support for `loo_subsample`
  * Fix `p_loo` calculation in sub-sampled PSIS-LOO-CV
  * Fix rounding of `subsampling_dse` in `compare()`
  * Honour circular in the Numba KDE
  * Fix _mcse_sd to use ESS of squared deviations
  * Fix custom limits for circular KDE
  * Fix Kaplan–Meier estimates for integer event times
  * Fix covariance and split steps in `loo_moment_match`
  * Fix `num_samples` default in survival curves</comment>
    <requestid>1392403</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
